.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt SEQ 1
.Os NovaOS
.Sh NAME
.Nm seq
.Nd print a sequence of numbers
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl w
.Op Fl s Ar text
.Op Fl f Ar format
.Oo Ar first Op Ar step Oc
.Ar last
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The first value and the step default to 1.
A negative step counts down. An empty range produces no bytes.
A nonempty range ends with a newline.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f Ar format , Fl Fl format Ns = Ns Ar format
Use one floating-point conversion from aAeEfFgG. Use %% for a literal percent sign.
.It Fl s Ar text , Fl Fl separator Ns = Ns Ar text
Write the separator between adjacent values. An empty separator joins their digits.
.It Fl w , Fl Fl equal-width
Pad values with leading zeros. This option is incompatible with an explicit format.
.It Fl Fl help , Fl Fl version
Print help or the component version, then exit successfully.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
seq 5
seq -s , 6 -2 0
seq -f '%.2f' 0 .25 1
.Ed
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 for invalid input or a write failure.
The step must be nonzero. NaN is invalid.
.Sh VERSION
seq (nova-cli) 0.20.0.
